---
import SectionHeading from "./SectionHeading.astro";
---

<section class="px-2 py-8">
    <SectionHeading boldText="Understanding" restText="the Problem" />
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-12">
        <p>
            The original product page was fragmented and hard to navigate. Key
            information like pricing and documentation was buried across tabs,
            leading to user frustration, low conversion rates and an increase in
            support tickets.
        </p>

        <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
            <div class="p-6 border-2 border-Charcoal rounded-lg">
                <ul class="flex flex-col gap-4">
                    <li>
                        <span class="font-mono font-medium">01<br /></span>
                        Tabs (Data, Documentation, Usage) fragmented the experience.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <span class="font-mono font-medium">02<br /></span>
                        Example data didn’t communicate the dataset and to download
                        it required a new window interaction.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <span class="font-mono font-medium">03<br /></span>
                        Product descriptions didn’t clearly communicate value.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <span class="font-mono font-medium">04<br /></span>
                        Pricing info was buried below the fold.
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div></div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="px-2 py-8">
    <SectionHeading boldText="Exploring" restText="Design Directions" />
    <div>
        <p>
            I audited the existing experience, analyzed support tickets and
            mapped the user journey to surface friction points. Interviews with
            users and internal teams revealed blockers around pricing clarity,
            content visibility and trust. These insights shaped early concepts
            and aligned stakeholders around key priorities.
        </p>

        <div>
            <figure>
                <figcaption>
                    Some sketches I created during my exploration phase
                </figcaption>

                <div class="swiper sketches">
                    <div class="swiper-wrapper">
                        <div class="swiper-slide">
                            <img src="#" alt="Placeholder" />
                        </div>
                        <div class="swiper-slide">
                            <img src="#" alt="Placeholder" />
                        </div>
                        <div class="swiper-slide">
                            <img src="#" alt="Placeholder" />
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </figure>
        </div>
        <figure>
            <figcaption>
                <strong>Wireframes</strong> that helped everyone stay on the same
                page
            </figcaption>

            <img src="#" alt="Placeholder" />
            <img src="#" alt="Placeholder" />
        </figure>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="px-2 py-8">
    <SectionHeading boldText="Crafting" restText="the Solution" />
    <div>
        <p>
            I audited the existing experience, analyzed support tickets and
            mapped the user journey to surface friction points. Interviews with
            users and internal teams revealed blockers around pricing clarity,
            content visibility and trust. These insights shaped early concepts
            and aligned stakeholders around key priorities.
        </p>
        <figure>
            <figcaption>Before & After</figcaption>
        </figure>
    </div>
</section>

